course: dictionary
lesson: 12232
title: Considerably: a big difference
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Considerably means a lot, or to a large degree. When you meet it, ask yourself: is the difference big? If it is, considerably fits. «The weather is considerably warmer today» means the difference in temperature is large, not just a tiny bit.
explain: Considerably is a formal word, so you will often see it in reports, letters and exam questions. Writers use it when they want to show that something is clearly noticeable. Compare «The train is a bit late» with «The train is considerably late». The second one tells you the delay is big.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in "a lot" or "much". If «The bag is considerably heavier» becomes «The bag is a lot heavier», the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Considerably means much, or a lot, to a large degree.
fact: «Prices have risen considerably» means prices went up by a big amount.
fact: Considerably often goes with a comparison word, like considerably bigger, considerably less or considerably more.
fact: In maths and science, considerably shows that two amounts are far apart.
fact: Useful phrases: considerably more, considerably less, vary considerably. «Heights vary considerably» means the heights are very different from each other.
exercise: «The new bridge is considerably longer than the old one.» What does considerably mean here? | Exactly the same length | Slightly shorter | *A lot longer | Painted blue
exercise: «Sam ran considerably faster than last year.» Which words mean the same as considerably here? | By a little bit | Quietly | *By a lot | Backwards
exercise: Why would a science report use considerably? | *To show a big, noticeable difference between two amounts | To tell a joke | To say that nothing has changed | To name a colour
test: «The lake is considerably deeper near the dam.» Considerably means | Near the water | *Much, to a large degree | Quietly | A little, hardly noticed
test: «Two plants grew, and one grew considerably taller.» Which phrase means the same? | a tiny bit taller | the same height | shorter | *much taller
exam: Ravi writes, «The temperatures vary considerably across the week.» What does vary considerably tell you? | The temperatures are written in a book | *The temperatures are very different from day to day | The temperatures never change | The temperatures are all the same
